// The public structs and enums left exhaustive, each with its kind
// (ticket 2096, ADR-0039). `cargo xtask api`
// (crates/xtask/src/api/exhaustive.rs) reads it.
//
// - A struct or an enum without `#[non_exhaustive]` breaks every game that
//   builds or matches it when it grows. Each one the head's listing shows is
//   listed here, under its crate, at each of its paths (a re-export is
//   listed at each), under its kind:
//   - `plain`: ADR-0039 kind 1, a value whose fields are its whole meaning
//     (`Pos`, `Rgb`), a newtype, or a unit struct;
//   - `closed`: kind 6's closed sets (`Dir`'s four directions);
//   - `private`: kind 8, a private field the listing doesn't show (or shows
//     as `_`), so no game builds it by literal;
//   - `open`: a type that may grow and hasn't moved yet. It moves under
//     ADR-0039 in the PR that grows it, with a `Breaking:` line. This list
//     only shrinks: the check fails an `open` path the base's file lacks.
// - A new type that may grow is `#[non_exhaustive]` with a constructor, and
//   stays out of this file.
// - The check fails a path the listing shows `#[non_exhaustive]`, or
//   doesn't show at all: take a moved or removed type out.
// - The paths are as `cargo public-api --simplified` names them, with each
//   crate's features of `API_CRATES` (crates/xtask/src/api.rs), without
//   generics or tuple fields. Several paths may share a line.
